<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sant Genís de Fontanes</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Saint-Génis-des-Fontaines</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sant Genís de Fontanes, in French Saint-Génis-des-Fontaines, is a former Benedictine abbey in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a>, founded in the early 9th century. Its marble lintel, carved with Christ in Majesty among the apostles and dated by its inscription to 1019–1020, is the oldest dated work of Romanesque sculpture in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. The abbey also keeps a reassembled Gothic cloister.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sant-genis-de-fontanes.jpg" alt="Sant Genís de Fontanes" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AC · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:St-G%C3%A9nis-des-Fontaines_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
